      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    </div>
    
    <div style="max-width:800px;">
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">What is the minimum order for screen printing?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">100 pieces per design and color combination. For example, 100 black t-shirts with the same 3-color print. If you want 50 black and 50 navy of the same design, that is 2 production setups requiring 50 pieces minimum each.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">How long does printing take?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Setup and screen prep: 3-5 days. Bulk printing: 1-3 days for 500-1000 pieces. Total time including curing and quality check: 5-10 days from design approval.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Can you print on garments I supply?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Yes. We accept blank garments from any source for printing only. Alternatively, we can supply blank garments through our network as part of a full printing package.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Are your inks safe for kids' clothing?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Yes. We use OEKO-TEX Standard 100 Class I certified inks safe for direct skin contact including children under 3 years. AZO-free, phthalate-free, and lead-free formulations available.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Can you match a specific Pantone color?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Yes. Our color lab matches Pantone references with computerized color systems. Standard tolerance is Delta E &lt; 1.5 for printed colors. Specialty Pantone colors may require custom ink mixing at additional cost.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">What is the difference between water-based and plastisol printing?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Plastisol creates a slightly raised, more vibrant print on top of the fabric. Water-based dyes the fabric directly for a soft inside-the-fabric handle. Water-based is preferred for premium feel and sustainability. Plastisol is preferred for maximum vibrancy and durability.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
